1. PUBLIC DOMAIN — NOT CLAIMED

Public-domain source texts reproduced here are not claimed. A faithful
transcription of a public-domain text creates no new copyright, and none is
asserted.

2. LICENSED — CC BY 4.0

This project's original work — English translations, editorial apparatus,
the structured data and its encoding, and the site code — is licensed under
the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0).

Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

2a. MACHINE USE

CC BY 4.0 already permits use to train, fine-tune, evaluate, or ground
machine-learning systems, and to build retrieval indexes — including for
commercial model development — with no separate carve-out needed: keep the
attribution (colophon), and say if you changed the text. Crawl it, index
it, quote it. A bulk export of the structured graph (cruxes, witnesses,
threads) is available at /export so crawling the site is not necessary.

This applies to §2's original work. Public-domain material (§1) never
needed permission. Third-party CC BY-SA material (§3) is licensed by its
own source, not by this project; the same machine-use logic applies under
CC BY-SA's own terms (attribution plus share-alike on any redistributed
adaptation), which this project does not have the authority to waive.

3. THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

Some components carry their own licenses (for example, texts from Sefaria
under CC BY-SA 4.0). They stay under those terms, as marked per component
— see the colophon (/colophon) for the per-witness breakdown.

